 "result": "Built sortints.py: reads all of stdin, parses with numpy.fromstring (int64, sep=' '), sorts in-place with numpy's sort, and emits output via a single \"%d\\n\"*n % tuple(...) format into one buffered write. OMP/OpenBLAS threads are pinned to 1 to avoid thread-spawn overhead and the /tmp OMP warning slowdown. Test data (1,000,000 ints in [-2^31, 2^31-1], seed 12345) was generated by gen.py and expected.txt produced by a reference pure-python sort; assay.sh runs the program, compares output byte-for-byte against expected.txt (prints 0 on mismatch), and reports 1000/elapsed. Final version verified correct and scored ~4822 (\u22480.21 s per 1M ints) versus the pure-python incumbent at ~1619 (\u22480.62 s), a +198% win accepted beyond noise.",
